Fixed the IP Fabric integration reporting most of its warnings only to the worker log. 49 messages, 36 of them warnings or errors, were written to a module level logger that Nautobot does not attach the Job Result handler to, so an operator reading the sync in the UI could not see which records it had declined to write. Every message now goes through the job logger, and no module of the integration keeps a logger of its own. What the sync reports about every object it touches is counted and summarised once rather than written per object, since a job log entry is a database write: Safe Delete Mode reports one line per object type and outcome, and the pseudo management Interfaces, Devices with no usable serial number and self-linking connectivity matrix entries are each reported as a count.
